  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef probstat_standard_errors(samples: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Standard Error Comparison** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef probstat_standard_errors(samples: list) -> dict:\n    ses = [round(float(np.std(np.array(s, dtype=np.float64), ddof=1) / np.sqrt(len(s))), 6) for s in samples]\n    return {'standard_errors': ses, 'average_se': round(float(np.mean(ses)), 6)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
